{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017zDFfB5dacXp4KvWgZ3kWm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/curriculum/blob/master/kcna/README.md\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:39:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation — cncf/curriculum repository, KCNA README\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"domain-weight-allocation\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# KCNA curriculum README — CNCF publication channel\n10\t\n11\tPrimary-source corroboration of the current four-domain weights, in the\n12\tauthority's own repository rather than on a marketing page. Supports Ch 19 §4's\n13\t— Dead Reckoning block.\n14\t\n15\t## Description — verbatim\n16\t\n17\t\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) certification provides a beginner friendly option to learn about the Kubernetes community and vast cloud native ecosystem of projects.\"\n18\t\n19\t## Domains and weightings — verbatim\n20\t\n21\t- Kubernetes Fundamentals: 44%\n22\t- Container Orchestration: 28%\n23\t- Cloud Native Application Delivery: 16%\n24\t- Cloud Native Architecture: 12%\n25\t\n26\tAgrees exactly with cncf-kcna-certification-page-2026-08-23.md,\n27\tlf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md, lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md, and\n28\tcncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23.md. Four independent CNCF/LF surfaces now\n29\tagree; the 44/28/16/12 split can be stated flatly.\n30\t\n31\t## Version and status — NOT STATED\n32\t\n33\tThe README contains no curriculum version number, effective date, or statement of\n34\tcurrent-vs-retired status. The effective date (2025-11-24) comes from the repo's\n35\tcommit history — see cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md.\n36\t\n37\t## Competency detail — NOT PRESENT\n38\t\n39\tThis README lists the four domains and their weights only. It does NOT enumerate\n40\tthe competencies beneath each domain. For those, use\n41\tcncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23.md or lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa3473e8-c724-44c2-96ab-1a38729efd99","uuid":"7832f96c-bbad-4eae-921e-95b315f4da24","timestamp":"2026-09-01T00:49:59.209Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/cncf-curriculum-kcna-readme-2026-08-31.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/curriculum/blob/master/kcna/README.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:39:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation — cncf/curriculum repository, KCNA README\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"domain-weight-allocation\"]\n---\n\n# KCNA curriculum README — CNCF publication channel\n\nPrimary-source corroboration of the current four-domain weights, in the\nauthority's own repository rather than on a marketing page. Supports Ch 19 §4's\n— Dead Reckoning block.\n\n## Description — verbatim\n\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) certification provides a beginner friendly option to learn about the Kubernetes community and vast cloud native ecosystem of projects.\"\n\n## Domains and weightings — verbatim\n\n- Kubernetes Fundamentals: 44%\n- Container Orchestration: 28%\n- Cloud Native Application Delivery: 16%\n- Cloud Native Architecture: 12%\n\nAgrees exactly with cncf-kcna-certification-page-2026-08-23.md,\nlf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md, lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md, and\ncncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23.md. Four independent CNCF/LF surfaces now\nagree; the 44/28/16/12 split can be stated flatly.\n\n## Version and status — NOT STATED\n\nThe README contains no curriculum version number, effective date, or statement of\ncurrent-vs-retired status. The effective date (2025-11-24) comes from the repo's\ncommit history — see cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md.\n\n## Competency detail — NOT PRESENT\n\nThis README lists the four domains and their weights only. It does NOT enumerate\nthe competencies beneath each domain. For those, use\ncncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23.md or lf-kcna-program-changes-2026-08-23.md.\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}}}
